-- ============================================================================
-- DRAFT / UNAPPLIED — DO NOT RUN THIS FILE
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Personal feed dispositions become durable — on `attention_user_state`
--
-- STATUS: draft. Never applied to any database — not production, not staging,
-- not a local instance. The lane that produced it (`audit/decision-memory`) is
-- PARKED as of 2026-09-02; see `docs/decision-memory-parked.md`.
--
-- ── Preconditions before this may EVER be applied ─────────────────────────
--
-- Every one of these, in order, and none of them is a formality:
--
--   1. Re-read the LIVE production schema of `attention_user_state`. This file
--      was written against a read-only capture taken 2026-08-28 and recorded in
--      `docs/decision-memory-consolidation.md` §1.1. The repo has no migration
--      for that table at all, migrations here do not describe production, and
--      four days is long enough for it to have moved.
--   2. Verify the columns. Every ADD assumes the current set; a column that has
--      since appeared with a different meaning (particularly `dismissed_until`,
--      which this file introduces deliberately distinct from `dismissed_at`)
--      changes the design, not just the DDL.
--   3. Verify the unique constraint is still `UNIQUE (user_id, attention_id)`.
--      `set_feed_disposition`'s ON CONFLICT depends on it, and its `WHERE
--      s.user_id = v_caller` guard exists precisely because a widened
--      constraint would otherwise let a SECURITY DEFINER upsert touch a row
--      that is not the caller's.
--   4. Verify RLS is still enabled and the four policies still compare to
--      `auth.uid()`. §6 recreates them; recreating a policy whose predicate has
--      since been deliberately changed would silently revert that change.
--   5. Verify the seven existing attention RPCs still exist and still behave as
--      documented — `acknowledge_attention` in particular is behaviourally
--      inert today, and a fix to it changes what this file should assume.
--   6. Verify `current_org_id()` still validates membership (migration
--      20260826100000). The org-stamping trigger here is only as safe as that
--      function.
--   7. Run `supabase/tests/feed-disposition-ownership.sql` against a
--      NON-PRODUCTION environment. It has never been executed anywhere. A
--      passing run on its own proves only that the test is wired to something.
--
-- Tested only in the sense that the SQL harness beside it was written to prove
-- this file's claims. No run has happened. Treat "reviewed" and "verified" as
-- different words.
--
-- ── Why this table and not a new one ──────────────────────────────────────
--
-- The feed's decision memory ("stop showing me this until…") lives in
-- `localStorage`. That is the wrong store for user state with a 180-day window:
-- it does not survive a cleared cache, does not follow a person to a second
-- device, and cannot be queried, so "what has this analyst deferred" has no
-- answer. The read path is `src/lib/signals/dispositions.ts`.
--
-- `attention_user_state` is already the general case of exactly this idea:
--
--   UNIQUE (user_id, attention_id)   -- i.e. (user, object)
--   snoozed_until timestamptz        -- a bounded personal window
--   read_state    enum               -- acknowledgment
--   RLS on all four verbs, every policy `auth.uid() = user_id`
--   seven SECURITY DEFINER RPCs that derive the user from the session
--
-- It was missing one caller, not a sibling. `attention_id` is opaque `text`
-- holding a 32-char hex hash (`generateAttentionId`); feed rows hold
-- `signal:<type>:<subject>`. Disjoint by shape, so the namespaces cannot
-- collide, and `computeAttention` looks rows up by exact key — a row in the
-- other namespace is never found and filters nothing.
--
-- A second table would have carried the same key, the same policies and the
-- same erasure entry, plus a standing obligation to keep two windows in step.
--
-- ── Live shape this was written against ───────────────────────────────────
--
-- Captured read-only from production 2026-08-28 and recorded in
-- `docs/decision-memory-consolidation.md` §1.1. The table had **0 rows**, which
-- is why every step here is additive and there is no backfill: nothing exists
-- to reinterpret. Every statement is `IF NOT EXISTS` / `OR REPLACE` so a
-- re-run, or a live shape that has since drifted, is not destructive.
--
-- ── What is deliberately NOT here ─────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- No investment judgment. `disposition_key` is the key `judgment-policy.ts`
-- classifies to derive a quiet window — feed mechanics. What an analyst
-- concluded about a position stays in `audit_events` as append-only history.
-- `intent` keeps that boundary queryable rather than conventional.
--
-- No shared state of any kind. Every row here is one person's view. Nothing in
-- this file can change what a colleague sees.
-- ============================================================================


-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. Additive columns
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- `dismissed_until` rather than reusing `dismissed_at`: that column is the
-- timestamp of the ACT and is permanent, with no expiry, and the attention
-- filter treats any value in it as "gone forever". A feed dismissal is bounded
-- — 30 days for `feed_dismissed`, 180 for `feed_not_useful` — so overloading
-- `dismissed_at` would turn a bounded window into a soft delete. Both columns
-- keep the meaning they already have.

ALTER TABLE public.attention_user_state
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS org_id           uuid REFERENCES public.organizations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS signal_type      text,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS disposition_key  text,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS intent           text,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS dismissed_until  timestamptz;

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.attention_user_state.org_id IS
  'Derived from current_org_id() by trigger, never accepted from the client. '
  'A user in two pilot organizations must not share one suppression namespace '
  'across both.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.attention_user_state.disposition_key IS
  'The FEED key (feed_snoozed, defer, not_mine, scenario_thesis_intact…) that '
  'judgment-policy.ts classifies to derive the quiet window. NOT the '
  'investment judgment — that is an audit_events row.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.attention_user_state.intent IS
  'triage | feed_quality | attention | judgment. Makes the personal/record '
  'boundary queryable: anything counting research must exclude the first three.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.attention_user_state.dismissed_until IS
  'A BOUNDED dismissal window. Distinct from dismissed_at, which is the '
  'permanent timestamp of the act and is read as a soft delete.';

-- `intent` is a small closed vocabulary; a typo silently mis-buckets analysis.
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM pg_constraint
    WHERE conname = 'attention_user_state_intent_check'
      AND conrelid = 'public.attention_user_state'::regclass
  ) THEN
    ALTER TABLE public.attention_user_state
      ADD CONSTRAINT attention_user_state_intent_check
      CHECK (intent IS NULL OR intent IN ('triage', 'feed_quality', 'attention', 'judgment'));
  END IF;
END $$;


-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2. The organization is derived, never supplied
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- The `quick_thoughts` rule (20260827090200), applied to a table that has never
-- had an org column. Supplying a foreign org is refused rather than silently
-- overwritten: nothing in the application sends this column, so a mismatched
-- value is a bug or an attack and both should be loud.
--
-- Unlike `quick_thoughts` this does NOT hard-fail when there is no active org.
-- Attention state predates the org column, its RPCs are called from surfaces
-- that work without an org context, and refusing the write would break
-- suppression for a user mid-onboarding. NULL means "no org context at the
-- time", and the read path treats NULL as visible in every org — which is the
-- pre-migration behaviour, preserved.

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.set_attention_user_state_org()
RETURNS TRIGGER
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public, pg_temp
AS $$
DECLARE
  v_caller uuid := auth.uid();
  v_org    uuid;
BEGIN
  IF TG_OP = 'INSERT' THEN
    IF v_caller IS NULL THEN
      -- Privileged, non-session write (service_role, psql, a seed). There is no
      -- session tenant to infer, so whatever was supplied stands.
      RETURN NEW;
    END IF;

    v_org := public.current_org_id();

    IF NEW.org_id IS NOT NULL AND v_org IS NOT NULL AND NEW.org_id <> v_org THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION
        'Cross-org violation: cannot write attention state in organization % from organization %',
        NEW.org_id, v_org
        USING ERRCODE = 'P0031';
    END IF;

    NEW.org_id := v_org;
    RETURN NEW;

  ELSIF TG_OP = 'UPDATE' THEN
    -- One exception to immutability: a row written before this migration, or
    -- while the user had no active membership, may be stamped once.
    IF NEW.org_id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.org_id THEN
      IF OLD.org_id IS NULL THEN
        NEW.org_id := COALESCE(public.current_org_id(), NEW.org_id);
        RETURN NEW;
      END IF;

      RAISE EXCEPTION
        'attention_user_state.org_id is immutable (attempted % -> %)',
        OLD.org_id, NEW.org_id
        USING ERRCODE = 'P0031';
    END IF;

    RETURN NEW;
  END IF;

  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS set_attention_user_state_org_trigger ON public.attention_user_state;

CREATE TRIGGER set_attention_user_state_org_trigger
  BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.attention_user_state
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION public.set_attention_user_state_org();


-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 3. The read index
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- The feed's only query is "my live signal rows", bounded by the `> now()`
-- predicates. Partial on the namespace so it stays small and so it cannot be
-- chosen for an attention-pipeline lookup, which has its own indexes.

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_aus_signal_live
  ON public.attention_user_state (user_id, org_id, attention_id)
  INCLUDE (snoozed_until, dismissed_until)
  WHERE attention_id LIKE 'signal:%';


-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 4. The write verb
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- SECURITY DEFINER, `auth.uid()` derived, `search_path` pinned — the standard
-- the seven existing attention RPCs miss (see §9 of the consolidation doc; a
-- separate migration should retrofit it onto those).
--
-- Upserts on the existing `UNIQUE (user_id, attention_id)`, so re-answering a
-- card replaces the previous answer rather than accumulating rows. That is the
-- correct semantic: a disposition is a current state, not a log. The log is
-- `audit_events`, and it is append-only precisely so this one does not have to
-- be.
--
-- The caller cannot name a user. There is no `p_user_id`, and there must never
-- be one: it is the only reason no policy in this file needs to defend against
-- a forged id.

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.set_feed_disposition(
  p_key             text,
  p_signal_type     text,
  p_disposition_key text,
  p_intent          text,
  p_snoozed_until   timestamptz DEFAULT NULL,
  p_dismissed_until timestamptz DEFAULT NULL
)
RETURNS void
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public, pg_temp
AS $$
DECLARE
  v_caller uuid := auth.uid();
BEGIN
  IF v_caller IS NULL THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'set_feed_disposition requires an authenticated session'
      USING ERRCODE = 'P0031';
  END IF;

  -- The namespace is enforced here rather than trusted from the client, so a
  -- feed write cannot land on an attention row and suppress a queue item.
  IF p_key IS NULL OR p_key NOT LIKE 'signal:%' THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'set_feed_disposition key must be namespaced signal:<type>:<subject>'
      USING ERRCODE = 'P0031';
  END IF;

  IF p_intent IS NOT NULL
     AND p_intent NOT IN ('triage', 'feed_quality', 'attention', 'judgment') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'set_feed_disposition: unknown intent %', p_intent
      USING ERRCODE = 'P0031';
  END IF;

  INSERT INTO public.attention_user_state AS s (
    user_id, attention_id, signal_type, disposition_key, intent,
    snoozed_until, dismissed_until, read_state, last_viewed_at
  )
  VALUES (
    v_caller, p_key, p_signal_type, p_disposition_key, p_intent,
    p_snoozed_until, p_dismissed_until, 'read', now()
  )
  ON CONFLICT (user_id, attention_id) DO UPDATE
    SET signal_type      = EXCLUDED.signal_type,
        disposition_key  = EXCLUDED.disposition_key,
        intent           = EXCLUDED.intent,
        snoozed_until    = EXCLUDED.snoozed_until,
        dismissed_until  = EXCLUDED.dismissed_until,
        read_state       = 'read',
        last_viewed_at   = now(),
        updated_at       = now()
    -- Belt and braces. RLS already restricts the row and `v_caller` is the only
    -- possible `user_id`, but this function is SECURITY DEFINER: if the unique
    -- constraint is ever widened, an upsert must still refuse to touch a row
    -- that is not the caller's.
    WHERE s.user_id = v_caller;
END;
$$;

COMMENT ON FUNCTION public.set_feed_disposition(text, text, text, text, timestamptz, timestamptz) IS
  'Records one PERSONAL feed disposition for the calling user. Takes no user '
  'id and can write no other user''s row. Never touches a shared investment or '
  'workflow object — the resolution verbs for those are separate and '
  'authorised separately.';


-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 5. Grants — `anon` loses a table it was never meant to hold
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Production grants full DML on `attention_user_state` to `anon`. RLS blocks it
-- in practice (`auth.uid()` is NULL, so `auth.uid() = user_id` is never true),
-- but this is the exact pattern the Quick Thoughts tenant work removed on
-- 2026-08-27, and this migration is adding columns that make the table more
-- interesting rather than less.

REVOKE ALL ON public.attention_user_state FROM anon;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON public.attention_user_state TO authenticated;

REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION public.set_feed_disposition(text, text, text, text, timestamptz, timestamptz) FROM PUBLIC;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.set_feed_disposition(text, text, text, text, timestamptz, timestamptz) TO authenticated;


-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 6. Policies restated `TO authenticated`
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- The four live policies are `TO public`, which means they are evaluated for
-- `anon` on every unauthenticated request. Same outcome, wider surface. Named
-- to match what production reports; recreated rather than altered so the file
-- is idempotent.
--
-- The predicate itself is unchanged and is already correct: `auth.uid() =
-- user_id` on USING and WITH CHECK alike. This is the line that makes user A's
-- dismissal invisible and unreachable to user B, and it is not being touched.

ALTER TABLE public.attention_user_state ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can view own attention state" ON public.attention_user_state;
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own attention state"
  ON public.attention_user_state FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can insert own attention state" ON public.attention_user_state;
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own attention state"
  ON public.attention_user_state FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can update own attention state" ON public.attention_user_state;
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own attention state"
  ON public.attention_user_state FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id)
  WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can delete own attention state" ON public.attention_user_state;
CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own attention state"
  ON public.attention_user_state FOR DELETE TO authenticated
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- No admin read path, deliberately. A platform admin has no business knowing
-- which cards an analyst snoozed, and `erase_user_personal_data` already lists
-- `attention_user_state:user_id`, so the new columns are erased with the row.
